@@ -24,6 +24,33 @@ debugging/reservation; those candidates are not a mutually assigned solution.
 Both functions and their geometry-rule/candidate types are available from the
 package root.
 
+`expandLocalSites: true` additionally samples conventional axis and diagonal
+sites within the source pad's half-pitch cell. It requires a drill diameter and
+keeps the drill outside the actual owning SMT pad; a land may contact that pad.
+Foreign pads, native vias and holes retain their configured clearance. Ground
+pour reservations allow a through-via antipad while remaining closed to foreign
+signal wires.
+
+## Mixed surface source prefixes
+
+`routeMixedSurfaceSourcePrefixesSteps` routes independent singleton boundary
+buses on the two actual outside copper layers. Supply prepared buses with one
+shared boundary and no explicit exit targets. The generator returns a complete
+set of `FanoutRoutePlan` objects, or `null`; yielded steps support incremental
+callers. The native layer count, obstacles, plane reservations and source ports
+remain authoritative.
+
+The planner reserves sources that cannot use a conventional opposite-side via,
+derives source-layer access from native geometry, and jointly selects the
+remaining via sites and boundary exits. Bounded provisional site revisions can
+recover a corridor blocked by an earlier legal local site. Fine-grid sampling
+keeps physical widths, clearance and full-span via dimensions unchanged.
+Every accepted source prefix ends at the boundary; destination routing and
+whole-board validation remain the downstream router's responsibility.
+
+`buildOutputSimpleRouteJson` converts accepted plans into supplied traces and
+boundary handoffs without removing the original downstream endpoints.
+
 ## Behavior
 
 - Uses `SimpleRouteJson.buses` when present. It also understands a point
